 # app
 
 The example.com/app backend.
+
+## Docker
+
+The image builds the server from `cmd/server` and runs it as a non-root user on port 8080.
+
+Build the image from the repository root:
+
+```bash
+docker build -t app:local .
+```
+
+Run it and publish port 8080:
+
+```bash
+docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 app:local
+```
+
+Check that the server is up:
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8080/healthz
+```
+
+To change the listen address, pass the `-addr` flag after the image name:
+
+```bash
+docker run --rm -p 9000:9000 app:local -addr :9000
+```
